# Review: SearchPlugin

The operations and surfaces are solid. `OpenSearch` and `SelectObject` are declared and handled.
`SearchDialog` and `SearchArticle` query the space's FTS5 index through `ObjectCombobox.searchQuery`.
The mailbox filters with the same `Filter.text(..., { type: 'full-text' })` and highlights matches.
The spec's data model is out of date: no `SearchQuery` or `MatchField` exists, and results are the
`SearchResult` of `@dxos/react-ui-search` (`id`, `label`, `snippet`, `icon`, `object`), with no
matched-field list. The debounce is the 200 ms default of `SearchList.Root`, not 400 ms.

The biggest divergence is the global filter (F-2). `SearchContextProvider` is mounted only inside
each search surface, so views elsewhere in the deck never see the query. Also, `filterObjectsSync`
pushes every object that has a text field without testing `match`, so the filter does not narrow
anything.

Of 22 items: 2 done, 7 untested, 2 partial, 5 diverged, 6 missing.

